WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
CMMC 2.0 uses three levels: Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.075
The levels connect information sensitivity and contract risk to increasingly rigorous

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:13.320
cybersecurity and verification expectations. Level 1 is called Foundational.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.805
It focuses on basic safeguarding requirements associated with Federal Contract Information

00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:21.335
and is based on the requirements in the federal contract safeguarding clause.

00:00:21.335 --> 00:00:26.155
Level 1 uses self-assessment and affirmation mechanisms under the CMMC program.

00:00:26.155 --> 00:00:28.030
It is not a promise that risk has disappeared;

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.840
the organization is representing that required practices are implemented within the

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.320
applicable scope. Level 2 is called Advanced.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.720
It aligns with the 110 security requirements in NIST SP 800-171 Revision 2 for protecting

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.760
CUI in nonfederal systems and organizations. Depending on the acquisition and contract,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.750
Level 2 may involve either a self-assessment or an assessment by an authorized CMMC

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.965
Third-Party Assessment Organization.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:55.375
The solicitation and contract identify the required status. Level 3 is called Expert.

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:59.975
It builds on Level 2 and adds selected requirements associated with NIST SP 800-172 for

00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:05.380
environments supporting higher-priority CUI and facing more advanced risk.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.995
Level 3 assessment involves the government assessment function defined by the CMMC

00:01:08.995 --> 00:01:09.580
program.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.690
An organization pursuing Level 3 must also satisfy the underlying Level 2 expectations for

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:15.920
the applicable scope.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.770
The practical lesson is not to choose a level based on preference or marketing language.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:23.975
Organizations should use current official requirements and the applicable solicitation or

00:01:23.975 --> 00:01:27.370
contract to determine the required level, assessment type, and timing.
